      "sourceTextSha256": "5528ef8635ad4fa1d1d852b4a84643ca218eb3142f35b9b9be5e4addefbf7479",
      "text": "Breakfast and transfer to the train station for the journey to the small town of Aguas Calientes, then a 30-minute bus ride up to Machu Picchu. This Inca city, a maze of finely built stone temples, houses and fountains, is spectacularly set on a ridge between two peaks; long hidden by dense vegetation, it was brought to international attention by Hiram Bingham in 1911. Guided tour, lunch in the afternoon and return to Cusco by train.",
